    <projectnotes visible="0" width="408" height="394" x="9" y="16" maximized="0" minimized="0"><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd">
<html><head><meta name="qrichtext" content="1" /></head><body style="font-family:'Verdana'; font-size:11pt;">
<p>Automation audio-truth fixture: one instrument track (&quot;Automation Target&quot;) with a 384-tick
MIDI clip of twelve notes, and a master mixer channel. Built so that automating a parameter changes
the rendered audio measurably - the notes span the whole clip, so a gain shape that is loud in the
first quarter and silent in the rest cannot render the same samples as the flat default.</p>
</body></html>]]></projectnotes>
